{title: The Lord Shall Return To Jerusalem}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{key: A}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 112}

Verse 1
The [F#m]Lord shall return to Jer[G#m]usa[C#]lem,
And [F#m]over all the earth shall [C#]reign.
Then [F#m]peace shall be found in Jer[G#m]usa[C#]lem,
As the [D]lion lies in [Esus]peace [E]with the [F#m]lamb.

Chorus
As the [A]waters flow where the [E]desert [C#]stood,
As the [F#m]heart of man seeks the [C#m]others' good,
They shall [D]know a new day is [A]dawning in Je[C#sus]rusa[C#]lem!
And my [A]heart cries out, "Even [E]so, Lord, [C#]come!"
Bring Your [F#m]peace and Truth; make each [C#m]heart Your home,
Enter [D]through the Gate with new re[A]joicing
Into Je[C#sus]rusa[C#]lem!

